    "guidance": "High-performing phase-routed option when semantic phase and the current red/goal/blue anchors are reliable. It passed 10/12 in-distribution runs. At the represented action-230 entry use drawer_clear; later use only the phase matching observed geometry: red_acquire for red approach/contact/lift, red_place_release for held-red transport through release and initial clear, bridge_to_blue only after release and vertical clearance, and blue_acquire for transit/approach/closure/lift on blue. Its phase-specific anchors are intended to address displaced red, goal, or blue, but no displaced-anchor validation exists. Prefer h02 if phase confidence is low. Avoid stale/noisy or fast-moving anchors, uncertain phase, obstructed/unreachable displacements, or assuming collision/contact recovery. Wrong-phase discontinuity, absent object/TCP co-motion, premature/failed release, crossing red before clearance, return toward red during transit, blue not under TCP at closure, drawer_position approaching 0.26, or IK non-convergence are failure cues. Both validation failures retained an open drawer (0.2723 and 0.2876 m) but ended with red off-pad; intermittent IK non-convergence also occurred in some passing runs, so pad containment remains decisive. Handoff: red_place_release may continue while red is held/touching in the successor overlap, followed by bridge_to_blue and blue_acquire; the clean nominal switch to blue_insert is after red is contained and stationary, drawer_position >0.26, and blue/TCP co-motion confirms initial lift."
  },
